       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 8000 mg four times daily comes to 32,000 mg per day. That is 10 times the maximum daily dose for ibuprofen, which is 3,200 mg/day in a monitored setting and 1,200 mg/day over the counter. A dose that high risks severe GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day)? That is the usual maximum dose. A more typical regimen is 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours, or 800 mg three times daily.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away. If you do want 8000 mg per dose, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional."
